WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.909 --> 00:00:03.440
They negotiated.

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:06.459
And then they negotiated some more.

00:00:06.459 --> 00:00:12.429
Eurozone finance ministers spent a total of
eighteen hours talking.

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:18.289
In the end, they agreed to this:
We have agreed to enhance the role of ESM

00:00:18.289 --> 00:00:21.600
(European Stability Mechanism) to further
strengthen the crisis prevention and resolution

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.390
capabilities of the euro area.

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:31.550
We will also increase the effectiveness of
ESM precautionary instruments.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:39.180
At the same time, we reaffirm that ESM support
is our last resort and that we need to ensure

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:42.780
an appropriate level of conditionality.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:47.180
In other words: more support for struggling
eurozone economies.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:50.770
But the help comes with strings attached.

00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:53.950
There was far LESS consensus on other issues
though:

00:00:53.950 --> 00:01:01.460
Like the proposal for a joint eurozone budget
and a plan to secure all euro zone bank despoits.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:06.130
Also looming over the meeting: uncertainty
over Italy's spending plans.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:10.610
The country is currently REVISING its draft
budget after the EU threatened to fine it

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:13.190
for violating fiscal rules.

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:18.110
Italy's public debt now stands at more than
130 percent of GDP.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:21.750
That's more than DOUBLE of what's allowed
under EU rules.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:02:42.480
Another thing that will need

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:57.610
to

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:39.510
be talked about.

